# --- Client-only (dynamic) SPA routes: rewrite to the app shell ------------
# Only surfaces that genuinely render on the client and must survive a direct
# link are listed here. Anything else falls through to /404.html, which
# Cloudflare Pages serves with a real 404 status (D11).
#
# /docs/* is deliberately absent: every real docs URL is a prerendered file,
# so a rewrite would only ever catch a typo and turn it into a 200.
# /dashboard/* and /admin/* rewrite to their own noindex shells rather than to
# the home page, so a deep link never inherits the homepage metadata.
# /blogs/* is deliberately absent. Cloudflare follows a _redirects rule even
# when a matching static asset exists, so a /blogs/* rewrite would shadow the
# prerendered post files this build writes (SEO audit issue 4). Unknown slugs
# fall through to /404.html, and a newly published post needs a rebuild before
# a direct link resolves.
/reports/*     /index.html            200
/report/*      /index.html            200
/playground/*  /index.html            200
/dashboard/*   /dashboard/index.html  200
/admin/*       /admin/index.html      200
